course: dictionary
lesson: 7096
title: Breaking down a word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word by looking at its parts. Peacekeeper is made of two parts: peace and keeper. A keeper is someone who looks after something, like a goalkeeper who keeps goals safe. So a peacekeeper keeps the peace.
explain: The word can mean a soldier or police officer sent by the United Nations to stop fighting after a war. «UN peacekeepers wear blue helmets and help keep a ceasefire without taking sides.» The clues are ceasefire and without taking sides: they stop the fighting and do not join either side.
explain: The word also means a person who calms arguments in everyday life. Test your meaning in the sentence: «The peacekeeper helped the two friends say sorry» still makes sense with the meaning "a person who calms arguments", so the meaning fits.
fact: A peacekeeper is a soldier or police officer, often sent by the United Nations, who stops fighting between groups after a war.
fact: A peacekeeper can also be a person who calms arguments and helps others make friends again.
fact: «Peacekeeping force» and «peacekeeping mission» mean a group of people sent to keep the peace.
fact: UN peacekeepers often wear «blue helmets», so people can recognise them.
fact: Ireland, Canada, Fiji and New Zealand often send peacekeepers, and they have worked in places such as Cyprus, Lebanon, South Sudan and the Congo.
exercise: In the word peacekeeper, what does keeper mean? | A person who sings in a choir | *A person who looks after or keeps something | A kind of tent | A person who plays football
exercise: «UN peacekeepers wear blue helmets.» What are UN peacekeepers most likely to be? | Football players on a team | *Soldiers or police officers sent to keep the peace | Shopkeepers selling food | Teachers in a school library
exercise: Sam says a peacekeeper can only be a soldier. Is Sam right? | Yes, because peacekeepers only wear blue helmets | *No, a peacekeeper can also be a friend who stops quarrels in the playground | Yes, peacekeepers never work with people | No, because peacekeepers are always in classrooms
test: «Ireland has sent peacekeepers for decades, including to Lebanon.» Which word shows that the help has lasted a long time? | Lebanon | peacekeepers | Ireland | *decades
test: Maya is a peacekeeper at her school. What does she most likely do? | She stands in goal during football matches | She wears a blue helmet and guards a border | She sends soldiers to other countries | *She stops quarrels and helps friends make up
exam: Which meaning fits peacekeeper in «The peacekeeper helped the two friends say sorry»? | A soldier who fights in a war | A goalkeeper who stops the ball | *A person who calms arguments and helps friends make up | A teacher who gives out homework
